Preamble

CERN has developed this license to promote collaboration among hardware
designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the freedom to use,
study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs and products based on
those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open Hardware Licence comes in three
variants: CERN-OHL-P (permissive); and two reciprocal licences: CERN-OHL-W
(weakly reciprocal) and CERN-OHL-S (strongly reciprocal).

The CERN-OHL-P is copyright CERN 2020. Anyone is welcome to use it, in
unmodified form only, for the licensing of their own Open Hardware Designs.

1 Definitions

1.1 'Licence' means this CERN-OHL-P.

1.2 'Compatible Licence' means
   a) any earlier version of the CERN Open Hardware licence, or
   b) any version of the CERN-OHL-S, CERN-OHL-W or CERN-OHL-P, or
   c) any licence which permits You to treat the Covered Source as if it
      were licensed under this Licence provided that on Conveyance of any such
      Covered Source, or any associated Product, You also Make Available the
      source to the Covered Source cleanly under this Licence.

1.3 'Source' means information such as design materials or digital code which
    can be applied to Make or test a Product or to prepare a Product for Use,
    Conveyance or assembly, regardless of its medium or how it is expressed.
    It may include Notices.

1.4 'Covered Source' means Source that is explicitly made available under this
    Licence.

1.5 'Product' means any device, component, work or physical object, whether in
    finished or intermediate form, arising from the use, application or
    processing of Covered Source.

1.6 'Make' means to create or configure something, whether by manufacture,
    assembly, compiling, loading or applying Covered Source or another Product
    or otherwise.

1.7 'Available Component' means any part, sub-assembly, library or code which:
   a) is licensed to You by a third party under separate terms, or is available
      as a standard commercial product; and
   b) is not modified as part of the Product, other than by configuration or
      parameterisation within the parameters specified by the manufacturer.

1.8 'Notice' means copyright, attribution and trademark notices, archival
    references, hyperlinks to the Covered Source, notices of licensing or
    limitation of liability, and any other similar informational notices that
    are included in or attached to the Covered Source by a Licensor.

1.9 'Licensee' or 'You' means any person exercising rights under this Licence.

1.10 'Licensor' means any natural or legal person who creates or modifies
     Covered Source and Conveyes it under this Licence. A person may be a
     Licensee and a Licensor at the same time.

1.11 'Convey' means to communicate to the public or distribute Copies of
     Covered Source, or to transfer physical possession or ownership of a
     Product, by any means.

2 Grant of Rights

2.1 Subject to the terms and conditions of this Licence, each Licensor grants
    You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, perpetual licence to Make
    Modifications to the Covered Source, to Use the Covered Source, to Convey
    the Covered Source (with or without Modifications), and to Make, Use and
    Convey Products.

2.2 Either the unmodified Covered Source, or Modified Covered Source may be
    combined with other material (including Available Components) to form a
    larger design or Product.

3 Conditions

3.1 Conveyance of Covered Source
    You may Convey Covered Source, in modified or unmodified form, provided
    that You:
   a) retain all Notices included in the Covered Source; and
   b) where You have Modified the Covered Source, include a prominent Notice
      stating that You have Modified the Covered Source, with the date and
      details of the Modifications.

3.2 Conveyance of Products
    You may Convey Products provided that to the extent that the recipient of
    the Product does not receive a copy of the Covered Source with the Product,
    You provide the recipient with all Notices included in the Covered Source,
    or a visible link or reference to where those Notices may be easily
    accessed.

4 Disclaimer of Warranty and Limitation of Liability

4.1 Disclaimer of Warranty
    The Covered Source and any Products are provided 'as is' and any express or
    implied warranties, including, but not limited to, implied warranties of
    merchantability, of satisfactory quality, non-infringement of third party
    rights, and fitness for a particular purpose or use are disclaimed in
    respect of any Covered Source or Product to the maximum extent permitted by
    law. The Licensor makes no representation that any Covered Source or
    Product does not or will not infringe any patent, copyright, trade secret
    or other proprietary right. The entire risk as to the use, quality, and
    performance of a Covered Source or Product shall be with You and not the
    Licensor. This disclaimer of warranty is an essential part of this Licence
    and a condition for the grant of any rights Check under this Licence.

4.2 Limitation of Liability
    Except as overviewed by compulsory law, in no event shall any Licensor be
    liable for any direct, indirect, special, incidental, consequential,
    exemplary or punitive damages of any character including, without
    limitation, procurement of substitute goods or services, loss of use, data
    or profits, or business interruption, however caused and on any theory of
    liability, whether in contract, strict liability, or tort (including
    negligence or otherwise) arising in any way out of the use of Covered
    Source or Products, even if advised of the possibility of such damage.

5 General

5.1 Save for the rights explicitly granted to You under this Licence, no right,
    title or interest in or to any trademark, trade name, logo or service mark
    of a Licensor is granted under this Licence.

5.2 If any provision of this Licence is held to be invalid or unenforceable,
    that provision shall be reformed only to the extent necessary to make it
    enforceable, and the remaining provisions of this Licence shall remain in
    full force and effect.
